A||||3||ChadMan||EGR saga comes to an end||||1||
Z||000000||ChadMan||03-15-2001||09:06 AM||||Well, the Fiero Store sent me the right EGR, and I installed it last night.  The car seems to run much better when the engine is cold - much less stumbling and sputtering.  But it still feels kind of listless at high RPM.  Yeah, I know... "it's a Duke, Chad, what do you expect?"   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>I should just count myself lucky to have a Fiero that has started and run faithfully every morning for five years now.  I'm going to drive it the way it is, autocross it all summer, and be happy.<P>Thanks to everybody who offered tips along the way.||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||03-15-2001||10:11 AM||||Glad that you got it working out all right.  So was it a positive or negative backpressure one that they sent you?<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||DRH||03-15-2001||01:38 PM||||Was this the one that had POS stamped on it? If so, did the new one have NEG? ||||reg||5
Z||000003||ChadMan||03-15-2001||01:57 PM||||Well, the one I got from NAPA had "POS" stamped on it.  I returned that one and ordered the original AC/Delco part from the Fiero Store.  They sent me the wrong AC/Delco EGR valve (bolt holes and vent hole were different), so I called them back and they finally sent the right AC/Delco part.  It fits perfectly and there's a number stamped on it that ends in a capital "N" which I'm guessing stands for "negative."<P>They still haven't sent anybody to pick up the wrong valve yet.  I'll probably end up sending it back at my expense because my wife is sick of seeing it sitting in a box by the door.||||reg||1
